    <div class="lux-brand-news-sheet"><header><p class="lux-brand-news-meta"><span>November 21, 2026</span><span>Product Story</span><span>LuxurEat</span></p><h1 id="lux-reader-title">Thai Durian and Italian White Truffle: A Surprising Way to Start the Day</h1><p class="lux-brand-news-intro">There is a special way to start the day: with the aromas of two distant traditions. On one side, Thai durian, a tropical fruit with soft, creamy flesh; on the other, Italian White Truffle, prized for its elegant, unmistakable aroma.</p></header><div class="lux-brand-news-copy"><p>Their meeting gives us TrufflElixir with Thai Durian and Italian White Truffle: an original syrup created to add an exotic, refined touch to breakfast, desserts and moments of indulgence.</p><section class="lux-reader-section"><h2>Inspired by sweet rice, coconut and durian</h2><p>In Thailand, durian lends itself to sweet, comforting dishes. For a breakfast inspired by local traditions, serve it with sweet rice and coconut milk, add fresh durian flesh and finish with a drizzle of TrufflElixir. The fruit’s sweetness and the coconut’s creaminess meet the aromatic notes of Italian White Truffle.</p><p>The syrup can also be enjoyed with waffles, ice cream, yogurt, cream and other desserts. Just a few drops add a distinctive aromatic touch.</p><figure class="lux-brand-news-media"><img width="1086" height="1448" srcset="<?php echo esc_url(get_template_directory_uri() . '/assets/media/brand-news/truffelixir-durian-pairing-720.webp'); ?> 720w, <?php echo esc_url(get_template_directory_uri() . '/assets/media/brand-news/truffelixir-durian-pairing.webp'); ?> 1086w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 767px) 100vw, 960px" loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="<?php echo esc_url(get_template_directory_uri() . '/assets/media/brand-news/truffelixir-durian-pairing.webp'); ?>" alt="TrufflElixir durian syrup served with durian sticky rice"></figure></section><section class="lux-reader-section"><h2>Durian’s nutritional profile</h2><p>Beyond its distinctive taste, durian has an interesting nutritional profile. According to USDA data for fresh or frozen flesh, 100 grams of durian provide approximately 147 kcal, 27.1 g of carbohydrates, 3.8 g of fibre and 1.47 g of protein. The flesh also contains potassium and vitamin C, as well as B vitamins, including thiamine (vitamin B1). Values may vary depending on the cultivar and degree of ripeness.</p><p>The result is a product that brings together the tropical sweetness of Thai durian and the aromatic richness of Italian White Truffle: an unexpected combination for anyone who enjoys discovering new pairings and turning breakfast into a flavour experience.</p></section></div></div>
